# Curvature from counting: general relativity from below, the 2D piece. See physics/curvature/check.py.
check "python3 -I physics/curvature/check.py"
frame "Regge 1961, curvature of a space glued from flat pieces sits at the joins as a deficit angle (cited from memory)" reading "2D fact only: a fan of d equilateral triangles has deficit (2 - d/3) pi; flat iff d = 6" -> 2 label checked-finite reach 3 cost 40
frame "Addison: flatten the cone into a disk (philosophy/cone.py); the link is analogy (reading), not checked" reading "the cone's apex is flat exactly when 6 triangles meet there; fewer is a positive-curvature tip, more a saddle" -> 2 label checked-finite reach 2 cost 40
frame "Gauss-Bonnet, discrete: total curvature is 2 pi chi (cited)" reading "every closed triangulated surface on at most 6 labelled vertices (218: spheres and the projective plane), the icosahedron and the 7-vertex torus: deficits add to 2 pi chi" -> 2 label checked-finite reach 3 cost 80
frame "The brain's hairy ball (biology/brain/BASE.md): index sum 2 on the cortex; the link is analogy (reading), not checked" reading "the 2 is chi of the sphere, the same number the deficits add to here over 2 pi; the brain side is tested, not exhaustive" -> 2 label checked-finite reach 2 cost 40
frame "Addison: general relativity given upwards from quantum gravity (Cheeger, Mueller, Schrader 1984: the Regge action converges to Einstein-Hilbert, cited from memory)" reading "the 4D continuum limit is not checked here; in 2D the total curvature is fixed by chi, so 2D gravity has no dynamics" -> none label open reach 3 cost 160
record physics/curvature curvature checked-finite "physics/curvature/curvature.ath: deficit angles in exact multiples of pi; a fan of d equilateral triangles is flat iff d = 6; on all 218 closed triangulated surfaces with <= 6 labelled vertices (1 + 10 + 195 spheres, 12 projective planes), the icosahedron and the 7-vertex torus, the deficits add to 2 pi chi."
